 -origin-y)\; } This welcoming watercolor class is designed for all levels.
  Guided by Nancy Ballard\, you’ll ease into the medium with simple\, app
 roachable techniques that take the fear out of painting. Through relaxed e
 xercises and encouraging instruction\, you’ll learn how watercolor reall
 y works—without pressure or perfection—while building confidence step 
 by step. Emphasizing play\, curiosity\, and small wins\, this class create
 s a supportive space to explore color\, brushwork\, and flow. Materials Pl
 ease bring: Your Watercolors Provided: Paper\, plus a mat\, backing\, and 
 sleeve so your piece will be ready for framing This class is located in th
 e PAC classroom.&nbsp\; About the Teacher:&nbsp\; Nancy Ballard 's love of
  art began in childhood\, when she first discovered the magic of brush and
  paint—a sense of wonder that continues to shape her work today. After a
  full life as a mother\, grandmother\, and corporate professional\, she re
 turned to art following her retirement in 2006\, studying watercolor with 
 Mary L. Harden at Strybing Arboretum. In 2009\, she was recognized as a Ma
 ster Artist of Botanical Illustration by the San Francisco Botanical Garde
 n Society. Nancy has also worked as a gallery curator and exhibiting artis
 t throughout the Bay Area\, sharing her botanical work in galleries\, wine
 ries\, hospitals\, and nonprofit spaces while supporting environmental awa
 reness through art. Learn More:&nbsp\; www.nancyballard.com #block-2edb6de
