 34b143f7637ca2730c1c { --sqs-block-content-flex: 0\; } #block-34b143f7637c
 a2730c1c { --opacity: 100%\; --translate-x: 0px\; --translate-y: 0px\; --r
 otation: 0deg\; --scale-x: 100%\; --scale-y: 100%\; --skew-x: 0deg\; --ske
 w-y: 0deg\; --origin-x: 50%\; --origin-y: 50%\; opacity: var(--opacity\, 1
 )\; transform: translateX(var(--translate-x)) translateY(var(--translate-y
 )) rotate(var(--rotation)) scale(var(--scale-x)\, var(--scale-y)) skewX(va
 r(--skew-x)) skewY(var(--skew-y))\; transform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(
 --origin-y)\; } Discover a simple yet powerful approach to painting by foc
 using on the three essential elements of successful artwork: drawing\, val
 ue\, and color. In this two-day workshop\, George will guide students thro
 ugh the fundamentals of composition and drawing\, including how to create 
 a strong focal point\, measure proportions accurately\, and lead the viewe
 r's eye through a painting. Next\, participants will explore the critical 
 role of value by painting with only Ultramarine Blue and White\, learning 
 how light and dark relationships create depth\, form\, and visual impact. 
 Finally\, students will unlock the secrets of color harmony using only the
  three primary colors and white\, mixing a wide range of vibrant palettes 
 while exploring warm and cool color relationships\, color temperature\, an
 d atmospheric perspective. Through demonstrations and a series of color st
 udies\, this workshop provides artists of all levels with practical tools 
 for creating stronger\, more confident paintings. This is an intermediate 
 painting&nbsp\;class. Students will be asked to bring their own material. 
 A list of required material will be provided to all students upon sign up.
  This class is located in the PAC classroom.&nbsp\; Two days\, 12-4PM each
  day. About the Teacher:&nbsp\; George Scribner i s an artist\, filmmaker\
 , and longtime Disney animator\, director\, and fine artist with more than
  35 years at The Walt Disney Company. Born and raised in Panama\, he direc
 ted Disney's animated feature&nbsp\; Oliver &amp\; Company &nbsp\;and has 
 earned international recognition for his large-scale documentary paintings
 . His major commissions include creating 35 oil paintings chronicling the 
 expansion of the Panama Canal for its permanent collection and a multi-yea
 r series documenting the construction of Shanghai Disneyland. Through his 
 work\, George combines masterful draftsmanship\, storytelling\, and a life
 long passion for painting and animation. Learn More:&nbsp\; www.scribnerar
 t.com #block-aba7662773e72679cc5e { --stroke-style: none\;--stroke-thickne
